{"id":4220,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/adverbs-manner/","parentId":540,"order":220,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Adverbs of manner (slowly) or adjectives (slow)?","seo":{"title":"Adverbs of manner (slowly) or adjectives (slow)? - Test-English","description":"Ace adverbs of manner with our A1 elementary grammar lesson. Clear charts, simple exercises, and practical examples make learning fun!","image":"/media/uploads/A1Grammar_Adverbs-manner.png"},"modified":"2026-06-04T07:17:10","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose adjectives or adverbs of manner to complete the following sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"489\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Complete the following sentences with the correct adjectives or adverbs of manner.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"490\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the sentences using adjectives or adverbs. Use the adjectives in the list and the adverbs formed from those adjectives.</h5> <div class=\"textBox\">clear –&nbsp;easy –&nbsp;fast –&nbsp;incorrect –&nbsp;patient –&nbsp;<del>quick</del></div> <p> <em>EXAMPLE: I need a <span class=\"textGap\">quick</span> answer.</em><br> <em>EXAMPLE: He answered my question very <span class=\"textGap\">quickly</span></em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"491\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Adverbs of manner</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18956\" src=\"/media/uploads/adverbs-manner-new.png\" alt=\"Grammar chart comparing adjectives to their corresponding adverbs of manner, including spelling changes and irregular forms.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Adverbs of manner: Use</h4> <p>We use adverbs of manner <strong>after a verb</strong> to describe the verb. We use an adverb of manner to say how something happens or how we do something.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>It rained <span><strong>heavily</strong></span>.</em> (=We are describing how it rained.)</li> <li><em>He always replies&nbsp;<span><strong>quickly</strong></span>.</em> (=We are describing how he replies)</li> </ul> <h4>Adverbs of manner: Position</h4> <p>We use adverbs of manner <strong>after the verb</strong> or, if there is an object, <strong>after verb + object</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>He drives <span><strong>carefully</strong></span>. </em></li> <li><em>She plays the guitar <span><strong>well</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Very, really, quite</strong></h4> <p>We can use&nbsp;<strong>very, really, quite</strong> before an adverb of manner.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>It rained <span><strong>quite heavily</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>He drives <span><strong>quite carefully</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>She plays the guitar <span><strong>really well</strong></span>.</em></li> </ul> <h2>Adjectives</h2> <p>We use <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/adjectives/\">adjectives</a> <strong>before a noun</strong> or after the verb <strong>be</strong>. </p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>This is <span><strong>an expensive guitar</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>This guitar <span><strong>is expensive</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h2>Adverbs of manner vs adjectives</h2> <h4>Difference</h4> <p>We use adjectives to describe a noun (before a noun or after&nbsp;the verb <strong>be</strong>), and we use adverbs of manner to describe a verb (after the verb or verb + object). Compare:</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Robert plays the guitar <span><strong>well</strong></span>.</em> (=We are describing the verb, i.e. <strong>how</strong> Robert&nbsp;<strong>plays</strong> the guitar.)</li> <li><em>Robert is a <span><strong>good</strong></span> guitar player.&nbsp;</em>(=We are describing the noun, Robert.)</li> <li><em>Sara eats <span><strong>slowly</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>Sara is a <span><strong>slow</strong></span> eater.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>Adjectives ending in <strong>-ly</strong></h4> <p>Some words end in <strong>-ly</strong>, but they are adjectives, NOT adverbs: <strong>friendly, lovely, silly</strong>. We CANNOT transform these adjectives into adverbs of manner.</p>","quizzes":[{"id":489,"questions":[{"id":4274,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Peter is a <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> driver. He drives very <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["careful","carefully"]},{"kind":"select","options":["careful","carefully"]}]},{"id":4275,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Turtles walk <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> because they are <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> animals.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["slow","slowly"]},{"kind":"select","options":["slowly","slow"]}]},{"id":4276,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>A <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> person usually speaks <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["cautiously","cautious"]},{"kind":"select","options":["cautious","cautiously"]}]},{"id":4277,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>; they are speaking <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["quietly","quiet"]},{"kind":"select","options":["quiet","quietly"]}]},{"id":4278,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Gordon plays very <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. He is a <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> player. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["good","well"]},{"kind":"select","options":["well","good"]}]},{"id":4279,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He did a <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> exam. He passed the exam <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["brilliant","brilliantly"]},{"kind":"select","options":["brilliantly","brilliant"]}]},{"id":4280,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We had <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> snow yesterday. It snowed <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["heavily","heavy"]},{"kind":"select","options":["heavy","heavily"]}]},{"id":4281,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He looked at me <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. He has a very <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> look.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["angry","angrily"]},{"kind":"select","options":["angry","angrily"]}]},{"id":4282,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We slept <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in our <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> bed.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["comfortably","comfortable"]},{"kind":"select","options":["comfortably","comfortable"]}]},{"id":4283,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He plays <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> because he is a <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> player.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["bad","badly"]},{"kind":"select","options":["badly","bad"]}]}]},{"id":490,"questions":[{"id":4284,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He normally drives very _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6132,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>slow</span>"},{"id":6133,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>fastly</span>"},{"id":6134,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>fast</span>"}]},{"id":4285,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I passed _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6135,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>easily the test</span>"},{"id":6136,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the test easily</span>"},{"id":6137,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>easy the test</span>"}]},{"id":4286,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The people in this company work very _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6138,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>hard</span>"},{"id":6139,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>hardly</span>"},{"id":6140,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>good</span>"}]},{"id":4287,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She is a _____ teacher.</div>","choices":[{"id":6141,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>well</span>"},{"id":6142,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>good</span>"},{"id":6143,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>goodly</span>"}]},{"id":4288,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>She teaches English very _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6144,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>good</span>"},{"id":6145,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>goodly</span>"},{"id":6146,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>well</span>"}]},{"id":4290,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You answered _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6150,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>correctly the question</span>"},{"id":6151,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the question correctly</span>"},{"id":6152,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the question correct</span>"}]},{"id":4289,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The article describes the situation very _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6147,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>simple</span>"},{"id":6148,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>simplely</span>"},{"id":6149,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>simply</span>"}]},{"id":4292,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They live _____ in Munich.</div>","choices":[{"id":6156,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>happy</span>"},{"id":6157,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>happyly</span>"},{"id":6158,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>happily</span>"}]},{"id":4291,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>After the break, we _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6153,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>finished the job easily</span>"},{"id":6154,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>easily finished the job</span>"},{"id":6155,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>finished the job easy</span>"}]},{"id":4293,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He didn't speak _____ English.</div>","choices":[{"id":6159,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>clearly</span>"},{"id":6160,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>clear</span>"},{"id":6161,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>well</span>"}]}]},{"id":491,"questions":[{"id":4294,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Please, can you speak <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>? I don't understand you.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4295,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He won the race. He ran very <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4296,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Your answer is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. Can you answer it again?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4297,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We were one hour late, but he waited <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> until we arrived. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4298,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>It was an <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> question. I answered it without thinking. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4299,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You answered the question <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. Can you answer it again?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4300,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Please, be <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> with him. He's young and inexperienced.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4301,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He's a really <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> runner. He wins a lot of races. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4302,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The water isn't <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>; it's dirty.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4303,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We climbed the mountain <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. We weren't tired after doing it.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}